The SELinux upstream userspacee project can now be found at http://userspace.selinuxproject.org. As before it is a wiki and bug tracking system dedicated to the userspace components of SELinux.

At the new site you'll find an updated release. The release tarballs and info are available at http://userspace.selinuxproject.org/trac/wiki/Releases. 

This is primarily a bug fix release with 2 notable exceptions in the development release: Ruby bindings for libselinux and Group support in seuser files.

For those who use the Git repository there are now tags for this release: 20080909 for the master branch tag and 20080909_stable_1_0 for the stable_1_0 branch tag.

